From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:37:38 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 164/297] Meridian: no crash where a space's tab has another
 profile than its window; links before the spaces load

Discarding a space tab made the replacement in the window's profile (a
CHECK); an app reparent from a space tab broke a same-profile CHECK and now
leaves the tab; windows open only when Chromium allows it (CreateBrowserWindow
CHECKs it, e.g. while quitting); a side panel the WebUI browser lacks no
longer CHECKs; a null sidebar service is no crash. A link opened before the
spaces loaded waits for them instead of being dropped; Boost's Improve finds
the AI set up in the main profile from a space tab too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
